+## Sync design checkpoint
+
+- Local Room DB remains authoritative for active Android use.
+- SQLite DB file is never synchronized directly.
+- Separate private GitHub runtime-data repository is configured by the user.
+- Protocol v1 uses a complete logical snapshot plus content-addressed media.
+- `inventory-sync/protocol.json`
+- `inventory-sync/current/snapshot.json`
+- `inventory-sync/media/<sha256>.<ext>`
+- Local and remote hashes/revisions are used to avoid unnecessary transfer.
+- Media is uploaded only if missing by SHA-256.
+- Concurrent local+remote change becomes a conflict; no silent overwrite.
+- Protocol v1 uses explicit source choice for conflict resolution rather than field-level merging.
+- GitHub token remains local and encrypted; it is never written to shared data.
+
+## Cross-platform rules
+
+- Shared coordination files must stay platform-neutral.
+- Android status never verifies Windows.
+- Windows status never verifies Android.
+- Android worker must not modify Windows implementation files.
+- If Android discovers a reusable product behavior, record the neutral behavior in shared docs.
+- If Windows later adds a reusable behavior, Android evaluates it from shared docs rather than copying Windows implementation code.
+
+## Testing rule
+
+Every new user-facing feature must have tutorial/testing guidance so the user can verify intended behavior.
+
+For v0.30 specifically test:
+- configure repository/branch/token;
+- first sync when runtime repository is empty;
+- first sync when runtime repository already contains inventory;
+- Android push then second-client pull;
+- second-client change then Android pull;
+- no-change sync performs no inventory/photo transfer;
+- simultaneous local+remote changes show conflict and do not silently overwrite;
+- photos round-trip correctly;
+- unsupported protocol/schema is refused safely;
+- token is not exported/shared.
+
+## Recovery rule
+
+If work becomes confused, recover from the verified v0.29 artifact. The v0.30 tree is only an in-progress checkpoint until the user compiles/tests and explicitly confirms it.
