+# Box Inventory v0.30.0
+
+Build 34
+
+## Shared Android/Windows inventory sync
+
+- Added the Android side of **Inventory Sync Protocol v1** for the cross-platform Inventory Box product.
+- Android remains a complete local-first application. It continues using its existing Room database and local photo storage; the SQLite database file itself is never uploaded or shared.
+- Settings now includes **Shared inventory sync** for a user-selected **separate private GitHub data repository**.
+- Configuration accepts `owner/repository`, branch (normally `main`), and a fine-grained GitHub token with Contents read/write access to that private data repository.
+- The token is encrypted with an Android Keystore AES/GCM key before it is stored locally. The token is not written into shared JSON files.
+- Startup performs a sync check after the local inventory is ready. While the app remains active, another check runs about every five minutes. **Sync now** is also available.
+- When both the local logical-data hash and the GitHub branch revision are unchanged, the periodic check ends after the lightweight revision check; it does not download the snapshot or transfer photos again.
+- Shared data is published as platform-neutral JSON plus content-addressed media under `inventory-sync/` in the configured repository.
+- Photos use SHA-256 content IDs so an already-present photo is not uploaded again.
+- GitHub media reads support both normal inline Contents responses and GitHub's raw response path for larger files.
+- Each shared media file is limited to 50 MiB in this protocol implementation, safely below GitHub's single-file hard limit.
+- Uploads publish required media first and `current/snapshot.json` last.
+- A snapshot is rechecked immediately before publish. If another client changed it while Android was uploading media, Android stops instead of overwriting the newer inventory.
+- Remote photos are downloaded and SHA-256 verified before the Room database is replaced. They are stored in separate imported files so a failed pull cannot overwrite the photo paths still used by the current local database.
+
+## First sync and conflict protection
+
+- If the configured GitHub repository has no Inventory Box snapshot, Android can publish the current local inventory as the initial shared snapshot.
+- If a snapshot already exists and Android has never synchronized with it, the app requires an explicit **Use GitHub** or **Keep this device** choice.
+- After a successful sync, Android records the synchronized logical-data hash and GitHub commit revision.
+- If Android and GitHub both change before the next successful sync, the app enters **Sync conflict** and performs no silent overwrite.
+- **Use GitHub** deliberately replaces the shared records on Android with the remote snapshot after confirmation.
+- **Keep this device** deliberately publishes the complete Android logical inventory after confirmation.
+- Protocol v1 intentionally favors data safety over automatic field-level merging. More granular merge rules can be added later only as a shared cross-platform protocol revision.
+
+## Shared data included
+
+The Android snapshot includes platform-neutral representations of:
+
+- boxes, QR identities, capacity, Location and Shelf/area;
+- item names, descriptions, quantities, categories, notes and box assignments;
+- favorites and In box / Loaned out / Missing state;
+- archive state;
+- serial/model identifiers;
+- purchase and warranty fields;
+- product/barcode/reference metadata;
+- primary/original/reference photos and additional-angle photos;
+- learned routes, custom categories and category aliases;
+- move history;
+- shopping-list records.
+
+Android-only preferences such as appearance, tutorial completion, navigation state, and the GitHub token stay local.
+
+## Cross-platform ownership
+
+- The existing Android application was **not** moved, renamed, reorganized or rewritten to create a new cross-platform source layout.
+- Shared product contracts/ownership documentation are maintained in the project coordination repository under `shared/`.
+- The future Windows implementation is owned by the PC/Codex agent and has its own status/baseline area.
+- Android v0.30.0 implements only the Android client side. It does not claim that the Windows implementation exists or is verified.
+
+## Tutorial/testing
+
+- Added **Shared Android/Windows inventory** to Settings → Tutorial & Help.
+- The tutorial covers creating a separate private data repository, token permissions, initial sync, first-sync/conflict choices, cross-platform verification, and the no-change/no-transfer check.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+- Room database remains **v12**.
+- Local `.boxbackup` format remains **v12**.
+- Existing v0.29 local data does not require a Room migration.
